/* ============================================================================
 * STRINGS — [ English, Español, Português ]
 *
 * Every user-visible string lives here. Written as parallel triples rather
 * than three separate files so a translator can see the source and both
 * targets on one line, which is how inconsistencies get caught.
 *
 * Spanish is Colombian-leaning, Portuguese is Brazilian, because those are the
 * two contexts the design is grounded in. Both are the languages the people who
 * would actually operate this speak; English is here for the wider
 * humanitarian-sector audience, not because it is the primary one.
 *
 * tools/check-i18n.js verifies that every key used in source exists here and
 * that no row is missing a language.
 * ==========================================================================*/
